WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.540
Every young athlete has people trying to help them.

00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:05.956
A coach sees one part.

00:00:06.116 --> 00:00:08.060
A parent sees another.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.556
But no one sees exactly the same child.

00:00:13.217 --> 00:00:16.553
A teacher notices something changing in class.

00:00:16.713 --> 00:00:20.553
And the athlete has a perspective none of them can supply.

00:00:20.713 --> 00:00:22.585
The same young person.

00:00:22.745 --> 00:00:24.617
Different moments.

00:00:24.777 --> 00:00:26.937
Different pieces of the story.

00:00:28.633 --> 00:00:30.601
Everyone is trying to help.

00:00:30.761 --> 00:00:34.577
But how do those pieces become a useful next step?

00:00:36.258 --> 00:00:40.674
That is the idea behind MORE Athlete, from MORE MindMap.

00:00:40.834 --> 00:00:45.836
A continuing AI coaching experience built around the young person, and designed

00:00:45.836 --> 00:00:48.754
to support the people helping them grow.

00:00:48.914 --> 00:00:52.682
This is the actual Athlete Consulting demonstration.

00:00:54.383 --> 00:00:56.495
It begins with questions.

00:00:56.655 --> 00:00:58.527
What matters to you?

00:00:58.687 --> 00:01:00.559
What helps you learn?

00:01:00.719 --> 00:01:03.791
What happens when things become difficult?

00:01:03.951 --> 00:01:07.023
And what do you want your coach to understand?

00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:12.869
MORE uses those answers to build a starting picture of the person.

00:01:13.029 --> 00:01:16.821
The Behavioral Operating System, or BOS.

00:01:16.981 --> 00:01:20.341
Here is Sofia’s actual example report.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:26.327
A whole person, with room for people, purpose, and choices of her

00:01:26.327 --> 00:01:26.813
own.

00:01:28.508 --> 00:01:31.628
The personality map is a way into the story.

00:01:31.788 --> 00:01:34.044
Each direction has value.

00:01:34.204 --> 00:01:38.771
It is not a grade, a verdict, or a prediction of the

00:01:38.771 --> 00:01:39.532
athlete’s future.

00:01:41.217 --> 00:01:47.495
The chapters explore how this person thinks, communicates, connects, and responds when

00:01:47.495 --> 00:01:49.065
life becomes difficult.

00:01:49.225 --> 00:01:54.676
The athlete can question the picture, add context, or say that something

00:01:54.676 --> 00:01:55.585
misses them.

00:01:57.258 --> 00:02:00.234
Nia’s report begins somewhere different.

00:02:00.394 --> 00:02:02.266
Fast to begin.

00:02:02.426 --> 00:02:04.562
Careful where it counts.

00:02:04.722 --> 00:02:08.418
The same architecture makes space for a different person.

00:02:08.578 --> 00:02:12.562
The goal is not to make every athlete fit the same description.

00:02:14.258 --> 00:02:19.884
Then MORE connects that picture to current reality through the Athlete Performance

00:02:19.884 --> 00:02:21.290
Assessment, or APA.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.322
Sport.

00:02:23.482 --> 00:02:25.354
Training.

00:02:25.514 --> 00:02:27.386
Warrior Mindset.

00:02:27.546 --> 00:02:29.418
And school.

00:02:29.578 --> 00:02:32.626
Four parts of a life, considered together.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.244
What are they trying to improve?

00:02:36.404 --> 00:02:38.276
What is working?

00:02:38.436 --> 00:02:40.308
What gets in the way?

00:02:40.468 --> 00:02:45.120
What does their coach see, and where does the athlete see something

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:45.508
different?

00:02:45.668 --> 00:02:50.060
The report keeps the person and their actual circumstances in view.

00:02:51.758 --> 00:02:55.838
Five Futures explores how the next weeks could unfold.

00:02:55.998 --> 00:02:58.278
Not a forecast of destiny.

00:02:58.438 --> 00:03:03.478
Possibilities shaped by what happens next, and signs worth watching.

00:03:05.175 --> 00:03:07.143
Then, one useful move.

00:03:07.303 --> 00:03:12.487
For Sofia, the proposal is to ask her coach to review one

00:03:12.487 --> 00:03:13.351
attacking choice.

00:03:13.511 --> 00:03:18.743
It connects her goals, her way of learning, and an existing practice.

00:03:18.903 --> 00:03:23.967
It remains a suggestion, not an agreement invented by software.

00:03:25.633 --> 00:03:30.097
Because the question is not simply, what should an athlete do?

00:03:30.257 --> 00:03:34.536
It is: what might help this athlete, in this situation, take the

00:03:34.536 --> 00:03:35.249
next step?

00:03:36.925 --> 00:03:41.989
The Athlete Consulting Tool brings that understanding into the conversation.

00:03:42.149 --> 00:03:44.885
Home, You, Your Sport, and Plan.

00:03:45.045 --> 00:03:49.527
The athlete’s BOS and APA are there with them, instead of starting

00:03:49.527 --> 00:03:51.021
from an empty page.

00:03:52.717 --> 00:03:56.833
You can explore the person, look at the sport, and consider a

00:03:56.833 --> 00:03:58.549
plan inside the same experience.

00:03:58.709 --> 00:04:03.372
The product you see here is the current synthetic demonstration; the wider

00:04:03.372 --> 00:04:06.869
youth and academy rollout is the vision being built.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:14.000
Imagine Mika, a fictional athlete, saying: I know what I want to

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:14.454
say.

00:04:14.614 --> 00:04:18.718
But when the game speeds up, I try to remember everything.

00:04:18.878 --> 00:04:22.790
MORE asks: what are you trying to remember in that moment?

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.822
Where to look.

00:04:24.982 --> 00:04:26.854
What to call.

00:04:27.014 --> 00:04:28.886
Where to move.

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:33.406
Now there is something worth exploring.

00:04:33.566 --> 00:04:38.208
MORE can help Mika and the coach discuss one clear cue to

00:04:38.208 --> 00:04:40.142
try in comparable practice moments.

00:04:40.302 --> 00:04:43.566
One manageable test, chosen together.

00:04:45.258 --> 00:04:47.130
What will we try?

00:04:47.290 --> 00:04:49.162
What will we notice?

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:51.194
When will we talk again?

00:04:51.354 --> 00:04:55.050
The athlete and coach choose the next step together.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:57.226
The agreement belongs to them.

00:04:58.925 --> 00:05:01.613
Then the next conversation begins.

00:05:01.773 --> 00:05:04.821
You and your coach agreed to try one cue.

00:05:04.981 --> 00:05:06.853
What happened?

00:05:07.013 --> 00:05:10.229
Mika says: it helped in the first drill.

00:05:10.389 --> 00:05:12.741
In the game, I forgot it.

00:05:14.425 --> 00:05:17.545
That is not simply a pass or a fail.

00:05:17.705 --> 00:05:19.793
It is something to understand.

00:05:19.953 --> 00:05:21.945
Did the situation change?

00:05:22.105 --> 00:05:23.977
Was the cue useful?

00:05:24.137 --> 00:05:26.009
Was it practiced enough?

00:05:26.169 --> 00:05:28.041
Did something else matter?

00:05:29.717 --> 00:05:34.865
MORE’s role is to help ask better questions, not turn one result

00:05:34.865 --> 00:05:36.581
into a final explanation.

00:05:36.741 --> 00:05:42.748
The continuing record keeps the agreement, the attempt, the observations, and the

00:05:42.748 --> 00:05:43.749
correction together.

00:05:43.909 --> 00:05:47.797
The next conversation has something real to build on.

00:05:49.467 --> 00:05:52.971
And the vision goes beyond one conversation.

00:05:53.131 --> 00:05:58.339
Imagine bringing the academy’s actual coaching methods into that experience.

00:05:58.499 --> 00:06:03.011
Making their expertise available when it is relevant to this athlete.

00:06:04.675 --> 00:06:10.540
Alongside it, MORE is designed to draw on carefully selected sport knowledge,

00:06:10.540 --> 00:06:15.427
and, as research capabilities are added, check relevant outside sources.

00:06:15.587 --> 00:06:17.459
A training question.

00:06:17.619 --> 00:06:19.803
A competition requirement.

00:06:19.963 --> 00:06:22.867
A new piece of research worth discussing.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:28.191
The purpose is not to put the entire internet in front of

00:06:28.191 --> 00:06:28.798
a child.

00:06:28.958 --> 00:06:33.038
It is to help bring the right knowledge into the right conversation.

00:06:33.198 --> 00:06:36.222
The academy contributes expertise.

00:06:36.382 --> 00:06:39.238
The athlete contributes experience.

00:06:39.398 --> 00:06:41.558
MORE helps connect the two.

00:06:43.258 --> 00:06:46.522
Now imagine what could happen over time.

00:06:46.682 --> 00:06:52.106
A coach discovers a question that helps an athlete explain a misunderstanding.

00:06:52.266 --> 00:06:58.403
Another finds that a familiar exercise is not helping, even with consistent

00:06:58.403 --> 00:06:58.914
practice.

00:06:59.074 --> 00:07:03.634
An academy begins to see where its approach needs to change.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:09.980
The long-term goal is to preserve and review lessons like these.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:16.399
With appropriate permission and privacy protection, selected lessons could inform a growing

00:07:16.399 --> 00:07:17.964
coaching knowledge base.

00:07:18.124 --> 00:07:21.100
Not another child’s private conversation.

00:07:21.260 --> 00:07:24.644
Not a list of supposedly perfect techniques.

00:07:26.342 --> 00:07:28.214
What was tried.

00:07:28.374 --> 00:07:30.486
In what circumstances.

00:07:30.646 --> 00:07:32.518
What happened.

00:07:32.678 --> 00:07:34.766
And what we still do not know.

00:07:34.926 --> 00:07:39.622
That could help another coach consider an approach they might otherwise have

00:07:39.622 --> 00:07:40.014
missed.

00:07:41.675 --> 00:07:44.627
Not: it worked somewhere, so do it.

00:07:44.787 --> 00:07:48.387
But: here is something relevant worth considering.

00:07:48.547 --> 00:07:50.779
Does it fit this athlete?

00:07:52.467 --> 00:07:54.339
That is the ambition.

00:07:54.499 --> 00:07:56.899
A growing body of knowledge.

00:07:57.059 --> 00:07:59.555
A continuing personal history.

00:07:59.715 --> 00:08:03.219
And support that still begins with the individual.

00:08:04.883 --> 00:08:11.411
Parents, teachers, trainers, and coaches could contribute where appropriate and permitted.

00:08:11.571 --> 00:08:14.859
Their perspectives stay identifiable.

00:08:15.019 --> 00:08:20.299
Disagreement becomes something to discuss, not something the software hides.

00:08:21.967 --> 00:08:28.657
And private development conversations do not automatically become academy reports or recruiting

00:08:28.657 --> 00:08:29.215
profiles.

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:33.623
Better connected does not mean everybody sees everything.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:40.817
As the AI improves, MORE can use better intelligence while preserving the

00:08:40.817 --> 00:08:44.036
authorized history that makes the relationship meaningful.

00:08:45.717 --> 00:08:49.149
We would build that future one stage at a time.

00:08:49.309 --> 00:08:51.181
Launchpad.

00:08:51.341 --> 00:08:53.261
Start with one academy.

00:08:53.421 --> 00:08:57.093
Find out whether MORE helps athletes and coaches.

00:08:58.758 --> 00:09:00.630
Playbook.

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:05.662
Prove the same foundation works with other coaches and academies.

00:09:07.342 --> 00:09:09.334
Academy O S.

00:09:09.494 --> 00:09:14.750
Help a whole program understand its development work and what needs attention.

00:09:16.425 --> 00:09:18.297
Athlete Passport.

00:09:18.457 --> 00:09:23.752
Give athletes a useful, permissioned record they can carry into their next

00:09:23.752 --> 00:09:24.193
chapter.

00:09:25.883 --> 00:09:27.755
Next Level.

00:09:27.915 --> 00:09:34.011
Connect selected, verified evidence with relevant college and development opportunities.

00:09:34.171 --> 00:09:37.699
Show what is known, and what still needs checking.

00:09:39.383 --> 00:09:41.255
Athlete Network.

00:09:41.415 --> 00:09:47.511
Connect participating programs, and carefully build knowledge from experience across them.

00:09:49.175 --> 00:09:53.663
Beyond Today Sports Institute could be where that journey begins.

00:09:53.823 --> 00:09:55.695
Start small.

00:09:55.855 --> 00:09:57.727
Prove it.

00:09:57.887 --> 00:09:59.759
Earn the right to grow.

00:10:01.425 --> 00:10:04.881
But the reason to build it is not the size of the

00:10:04.881 --> 00:10:05.169
network.

00:10:05.329 --> 00:10:08.449
It is the young person standing in front of us.

00:10:08.609 --> 00:10:10.481
Who wants to improve.

00:10:10.641 --> 00:10:12.657
Who deserves to be heard.

00:10:14.342 --> 00:10:18.201
Who should be able to say, that is not quite right, and

00:10:18.201 --> 00:10:19.166
be taken seriously.

00:10:19.326 --> 00:10:24.577
Imagine support that remembers the work, respects the person, and keeps looking

00:10:24.577 --> 00:10:26.766
for a better next step.

00:10:28.467 --> 00:10:31.611
Not to decide who they must become.

00:10:31.771 --> 00:10:34.771
To help them pursue the future they choose.

00:10:36.467 --> 00:10:38.339
Understand the person.

00:10:38.499 --> 00:10:40.371
Support the journey.

00:10:40.531 --> 00:10:42.451
Build on what we learn.
